<article class="env-lemma" id="092H">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/092H">Lemma <span data-tag="092H">15.106.7</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ and $A \to A'$ be ring maps. Let $B' = B \otimes _ A A'$ be the base change of $B$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $B \otimes _ A B \to B$ is flat, then $B' \otimes _{A'} B' \to B'$ is flat. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $A \to B$ is weakly étale, then $A' \to B'$ is weakly étale. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume $B \otimes _ A B \to B$ is flat. The ring map $B' \otimes _{A'} B' \to B'$ is the base change of $B \otimes _ A B \to B$ by $A \to A'$. Hence it is flat by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00HI" data-tag="00HI">10.39.7</a>. This proves (1). Part (2) follows from (1) and the fact (just used) that the base change of a flat ring map is flat. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>